    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/lecturer-college-of-arts-and-sciences-biology-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - College of Arts and Sciences, Biology - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Lecturer - College of Arts and Sciences, Biology San Diego, California Faculty 4795 Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Biology seeks broadly trained biologists capable of teaching introductory biology majors courses such as Bioenergetics and Ecosystems and Genomes and Evolution (lecture or lab sections). This position is included in the Non-tenure Track Bargaining Unit, and the successful applicant employee, subject to the terms of the College’s Collective Bargaining will be a bargaining unit Agreement with SEIU Local 721. Assignments to these courses are considered lecturer and non-benefit based. Each course consists of 3 units of teaching credit and the maximum allowable for each non-benefits based instructor is 6 units. Episodic need during Fall semesters (Sept -Dec) or Spring semesters (end Jan- May). $2,500 - $2,575 per unit Vacancies in this department may not currently exist but may become available at any point while this announcement is open.  Your resume and any supporting application materials will be retained and reviewed as vacancies become available. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d2e875db Last Name (required) 0595f206 Email (required) 541fd336 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0ce5650f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts and Sciences Expression of Interest College of Arts and Sciences Expression of Interest Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) a4bb506b Last Name (required) 9e261f0e Email (required) 61d20ec4 Send Please wait... Done Not