    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/open-rank-assistant-associate-or-full-professor-of-english-and-writing-program-director-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director",
      "description": "Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director San Diego, California Faculty Full-time regular Closing on: Nov 1 2026 5668 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director\n\n\nPosting # 5668 Department Description: The Department of English at the University of San Diego, housed within the College of Artsand Sciences, is a multidisciplinary Department that features courses in domestic and global literatures, literary cultures and theories, and creative writing. The Department also houses the University’s First Year Writing Program. The College of Arts and Sciences is at the heart of the University of San Diego. Our philosophy is built on the enduring values of the Catholic intellectual tradition, immersing students in the concepts of free inquiry, ethical conduct and compassionate service. The College aims to establish an academic foundation for students to thrive and gain a comprehensive education, which spans the sciences, arts and social sciences. Through our exemplary liberal arts education and rigorous scholarship, we aspire to not only educate the mind but also develop the whole person. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Department of English at the University of San Diego invites applications for the position of Director of the University Writing Program to begin in Fall of 2027. We seek applicants at the level of advanced assistant, associate, or full professor of English. The teaching assignment is four courses per year. Teaching responsibilities include writing and literature courses at all levels. Administrative responsibilities include collaboration with faculty and administration in overseeing USD’s Writing Program; supervision of first-year writing courses; contributing to personnel decisions (in consultation with English department chair); incoming student assessment and competency exams; coordinating all upper division, cross-curricular writing courses, including training faculty, reviewing Core Advanced Writing-course applications and syllabi; offering training workshops for all Writing Program faculty; Writing Program assessment; oversight of English for Speakers of Other Languages student assessment and support programming. Job Requirements: The successful candidate will be a writing specialist with a PhD in English, Rhetoric and Composition, or a related field, with meaningful preparation in English literature preferred, and an interest in Creative Writing welcome. Substantial experience in Writing Program leadership administration, background in working with Writing Across the Curriculum and Writing in the Disciplines; Writing Program assessment; Writing Centers; and English for Speakers of Other Languages programs also required. Significant record of publication and research in the field expected. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Posting salary: $6,931.25-$11,666.67 monthly: Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Please submit all materials by Sunday, October 4, 2026 Application materials must include: A cover letter of application, which should express: A philosophy of writing pedagogy (particularly in an age of GenAI), including concrete examples of the ways that those principles have been implemented in teaching, research, and writing program administration. The candidate’s plans for service, commitment to the University mission, and inclusivity in teaching, research, and Writing Program Administration. Curriculum Vitae Research statement and sample of scholarly or, if applicable, creative work Teaching statement and sample syllabi that indicate an ability and willingness to teach reading and writing as twinned skills, as well as a discussion of the candidate’s commitment to inclusive pedagogy A one-page statement of vision for the writing program at USD Contact information for three references who will be sent a link to upload letters. Please contact Professor Brad Melekian, English Department Chair and Search Committee Chair, with any questions, at melekian@sandiego.edu . If you have any technical difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) f857d6d6 Last Name (required) b4d32053 Email (required) fae730ce Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 1f8d04c0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts and Sciences Faculty College of Arts and Sciences Faculty Employment Type Faculty Full-time regular Faculty Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 726c6af3 Last Name (required) 6568ea1c Email (required) 8d1b67b9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
