    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-marketing-and-communications-san-diego-california-united-states-f4356890-71b8-42ed-bb16-db0e39849a2a": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications San Diego, California Full-time regular 5723 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications; Athletics\n\n\nPosting # 5723 Department Description: As part of the University of San Diego, a Roman Catholic University, the Department of Intercollegiate Athletics is committed to advancing academic and athletic excellence and enhancing students' lives while promoting the University of San Diego. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications serves as the primary marketing and fan engagement leads for assigned athletics programs. This role is responsible for developing and executing sport-specific marketing strategies designed to increase attendance, enhance the fan experience, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and support departmental revenue generation efforts. In addition to leading marketing initiatives, this position provides secondary support in storytelling, digital content coordination, and limited sports information responsibilities when needed. This role works collaboratively within the External Affairs unit to ensure unified messaging, strong brand alignment, and effective fan engagement across all athletics platforms. Duties and Responsibilities: Marketing, Fan Engagement & Digital Strategy Serve as the primary marketing lead for assigned sports programs and secondary support for additional teams. Develop and execute sport-specific marketing plans focused on: Attendance growth Fan engagement Brand awareness Revenue support initiatives Plan and execute game-day marketing initiatives, promotions, and fan engagement activities. Coordinate in-game entertainment, promotions, and student engagement efforts. Assist with departmental initiatives including Kids Club, group experiences, and community engagement programs. Assist with digital marketing initiatives across social media, web, email, and paid marketing platforms. Coordinate promotional email campaigns supporting attendance, fan engagement, and departmental initiatives. Help grow and engage fan databases through digital marketing initiatives. Utilize analytics and audience insights to help guide campaign strategy and performance. Work collaboratively with coaches and sport administrators to align marketing efforts with program goals. Storytelling & Creative Collaboration Collaborate with creative services staff to develop compelling storytelling content. Identify and amplify stories featuring student-athletes, coaches, and program achievements. Support department-wide storytelling initiatives that elevate the USD Athletics brand. Coordinate with creative staff to ensure consistent messaging and brand presentation across all athletics platforms. Assist in the planning and execution of digital content strategies across social, video, and web platforms. Collaborate on feature content, behind-the-scenes storytelling, and brand-building initiatives for assigned programs. Support creative ideation and campaign development tied to major athletics initiatives and events. Administrative & External Affairs Collaboration Assist with department-wide external affairs initiatives and special projects. Support collaboration between marketing, creative services, ticketing, sponsorship, and merchandise units. Assist with event planning, promotional logistics, and operational coordination as assigned. Certificates, Licenses, Registrations: CPR/first aid certification required within six weeks of employment California driver’s license required. Special Conditions of Employment: Must be available to work some evenings and weekends due to working home and away events. This position requires occasional travel, including to away events. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required, preferably in Communications, Marketing, or Journalism. Minimum one year of experience in Sports Communications or Sports Marketing required; two or more years preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Understanding of NCAA rules and regulations strongly preferred. Working proficiency with SIDEARM Sports, StatCrew, NCAA Genius/NCAA Manager, StatBroadcast, Adobe Photoshop, and Adobe InDesign strongly preferred. Experience with still photography preferred. Performance Expectations - Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong communication and writing abilities Strong organizational and project management skills Ability to manage multiple sports and priorities simultaneously Collaborative and team-oriented mindset Ability to communicate, orally and in writing, with local media, USD employees, and national media outlets. Excellent organization skills. Ability to work independently, or with others, under pressure and meet deadlines. Excellent writing, oral and computer skills. Understanding of sports and statistics. Excellent skills in the use of specific equipment and tools as identified below. Knowledgeable with video equipment and post production software for video editing. Functional knowledge of video streaming and elements of a live sports video production/broadcast. Sports marketing and fan engagement Digital and email marketing strategy Creative collaboration and storytelling Ability to make data-informed decisions Posting Salary: $5,858.67 - $6,083.33 per month; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume and Cover Letter Required Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application. In addition, please upload a cover letter and resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: Hours: 40 hours per week Closing date: Open until filled Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 207283cc Last Name (required) 70747d3f Email (required) d1e82e29 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 29fde907 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrator Athletics Administrator Athletics Employment Type Full-time regular Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 8c2172c4 Last Name (required) 5aebfb78 Email (required) c5c08713 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
