    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-creative-services-revenue-and-supportive-content-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Creative Services (Revenue and Supportive Content)",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Creative Services (Revenue and Supportive Content) - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Assistant Director of Creative Services (Revenue and Supportive Content) San Diego, California Full-time regular 5711 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Assistant Director of Creative Services (Revenue and Supportive Content); Athletics\n\n\nPosting # 5711 Department Description:\nAs part of the University of San Diego, a Roman Catholic University, the Department of Intercollegiate Athletics is committed to advancing academic and athletic excellence and enhancing students' lives while promoting the University of San Diego.\n\n\nUniversity Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Assistant Director of Creative Services (Revenue Content) serves as the department's primary creative producer focused on revenue-generating initiatives. This position is responsible for producing high-quality video, photography, graphic design and digital content that supports ticket sales, sponsorship activation, development, fan engagement and the overall growth of the USD Athletics brand. The position will be assigned and responsible for specific sports, while keeping the revenue generation priorities at the forefront. Working collaboratively with marketing and communications, sports information, sponsorship, ticket sales and external partners, this position develops compelling visual storytelling while prioritizing projects that directly contribute to departmental revenue goals. Duties and Responsibilities: Revenue Marketing & Sponsorship Creative Produce video, graphic and digital assets supporting season tickets, group sales and single-game ticket campaigns. Develop creative materials for sponsorship sales presentations and partnership proposals. Create sponsor fulfillment assets including social graphics, in-venue creative, digital advertisements, ESPN+ promotional content. Produce behind-the-scenes content that increases fan engagement and drives revenue opportunities. Collaborate with JMI Sports and internal revenue staff to develop partnership assets. Collaborate with the development unit to support fundraising efforts for USD Athletics. Photography & Videography Capture photography and video at athletic events, practices, community appearances and special events. Produce promotional videos highlighting student-athletes, coaches, facilities and the USD Athletics experience. Manage editing, color correction, motion graphics and final production of video projects. Build and maintain a department-wide digital asset library. Sport Support & External Initiatives Recruit, train, and manage a team of student workers and marketing interns. Support assigned sports with creative content throughout the year. Assist marketing and communications team with major campaigns, championships and special events. Collaborate on content planning surrounding key athletic initiatives and departmental priorities. Graphic Design & Digital Content Design graphics for social media, marketing campaigns, digital advertising and athletic promotions. Develop templates that improve efficiency for recurring sponsorship and marketing initiatives. Assist with creative direction for new branding campaigns and revenue-focused storytelling. Ensure brand consistency across all visual communications. Administrative & Other Duties Assist with creative planning meetings and project timelines. Manage equipment and creative production workflow. Stay current on creative trends, software and best practices. Perform other duties as assigned. Special Conditions of Employment: Must be able to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed in support of athletic events. Required to travel to select off-campus events. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum one (1) year of relevant experience in marketing, promotions or a related field is required. Experience working in college athletics, live event operations, or related environments. Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Two or more years of experience in sports marketing or event presentation preferred. Knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Premiere) and/or other creative tools. Familiarity with game production software such as Sound Director. Supervisory experience with student staff or interns. Posting Salary: $5,858.67-$6,000 per month; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume and Cover Letter Required Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application. In addition, please upload a cover letter and resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: Hours: 40 hours per week Closing date: Open until filled Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 29715cfa Last Name (required) e158d9e8 Email (required) 67a816db Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 499366eb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrator Athletics Administrator Athletics Employment Type Full-time regular Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 9e80c716 Last Name (required) f7bb8f20 Email (required) 9b9f2c00 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential