    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/tram-driver-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Tram Driver",
      "description": "Tram Driver - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Tram Driver San Diego, California Full-time temporary 5692 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Tram Driver; Tram Services\n\n\nPosting # 5692 Department Description: The Tram Service is an on-campus shuttle service that moves students, faculty, staff and visitors to various stops on the campus. The trams run in a circular loop throughout the entire campus as well as short loops to media reaccommodate heavier traffic from Manchester Village and the West Parking Structure. The Tram Service also provides morning and evening service to Old Town Trolley Station. The Tram Service operates full time during the fall and spring semesters and on a limited basis during intersession and summer. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: This is a full-time, temporary, benefit-based position with an anticipated end date of June 1, 2027. The appointment is renewable at the discretion of the University and dependent upon performance and continued funding. The tram driver supports the University and department mission to offer quality service and create a welcoming environment. Under supervision, this position is responsible for the operation of a tram designed to carry up to 30 passengers on and off campus. Duties and Responsibilities: Tram Operations: Drives tram on designated routes. Maintains current Class B driver’s license with passenger endorsement of 30+ and medical certification. Adheres to all traffic regulations. Drives in a safe and efficient manner. Maintains scheduled runs. Displays courteous manners to all passengers. Checks vehicle for damage and maintenance needs (tires, cleanliness). Helps maintain vehicle cleanliness. Practices non-aggressive, defensive driving techniques; anticipates and reports traffic problems to other drivers. Monitors gauges, reports discrepancies, and initiates correction. Monitors and responds to communications over radio. Maintains current knowledge of applicable safety procedures and emergency equipment in the event of an illness, accident, or breakdown. Makes oneself familiar and adheres to University polices in regards to Standards of Conduct. Follows safety practices appropriate to the trade and complies with rules and regulations established by the University, state and federal agencies. Performs other duties as assigned by supervisor. Certificates, Licenses, Registrations: Must have a valid, California class B driver’s license with passenger endorsement of 30 or more. Must maintain current medical certificate. Special Conditions of Employment: Successfully pass drug-screening test. Must pass Department of Motor Vehicles background check and submit driver record printout. Must be able to work assigned hours and may be required to work overtime and weekends, as needed. May need to adjust shifts; work extended or late shifts. Job hours and/or work week may be changed when necessary to meet work commitments. Must have a valid, California Class B driver’s license with passenger endorsement of 30 or more and will be required to drive University vehicles. Employee is required to properly wear a uniform issued by USD. Will participate in the University and/or department leadership enrichment courses and/or seminars related to the trade. Due to safety sensitive job classification, must pass drug and alcohol pre-employment exam and enroll in random testing program. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Minimum of a high school diploma or equivalent. Minimum of three years’ operating with a Class B license with passenger endorsement of 30 or more. Performance Expectations - Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Must be able to clearly communicate information to a wide variety of people, as well as the ability to handle problem passengers. Physical strength and mobility to assist with passengers who use a wheelchair. Skill in driving vehicles in pedestrian congested areas. Knowledge of various safe-driving techniques. Must become familiar with campus building names to help direct visitors. Be knowledgeable of campus layout and parking facilities. Must maintain an acceptable attendance record. Posting Salary: $22.24 - $22.25 per hour; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume Required Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application and, for full consideration, please upload a resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: 37. 5 Hours per week Closing date: Open until filled Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) b95fcbca Last Name (required) 2ce910f3 Email (required) 391aa944 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b9b0af16 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Tram Services Staff Tram Services Employment Type Full-time temporary Full-time temporary Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 3007062b Last Name (required) 99f5bb93 Email (required) 810741b4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
